{% extends "base.html.jinja" %}
{% block title %}How to file a claim — Significance{% endblock %}
{% block content %}<section class="band prose-page"><p class="lbl">How to file a claim</p>
<p>These details make a proof claim easier for other people to pick up, whether it appears on a forum, in an arXiv comment, or here.</p>
<ol><li>State the theorem exactly, with its definitions named.</li><li>Give the document a fixed identity: link and SHA-256 of the PDF.</li><li>List the papers, results, and prior claims you build on, with versions.</li><li>Say what you did not check, and which tools you used and for what.</li><li>Name the parts you consider risky.</li></ol>
<p class="lbl">Copyable template</p><pre class="copy-status-text">Claim:
Document URL:
Document SHA-256:
Builds on (with versions):
I did not check:
Tools used and purpose:
Parts I consider risky:</pre>
<div class="next-action">
<p class="lbl">When you are ready</p>
<p>Send the filled template with one link to the claim or paper.</p>
<p><a class="button" href="{{ links.request }}">Request or correct a record</a></p>
<p class="meta">The advanced contributor builder is for maintainers and technical contributors; you do not need it to submit a claim.</p>
</div>
</section>{% endblock %}
